 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you doing these days? Use a can wire mesh cage around each bag, bear proof bin covers, or store the food in your tent. Which do you think bears respect most? Keep them in the tent with you, or at least in your sleepout under an overhead tarp. A sleeping bag inside a bear bag is very warm, and bears respect tents. Make a clear, loud noise, wave sticks, and back away. Then pack up and go far away. Bears learn quickly, and the last thing we want is one getting used food from hikers. You' got this. Bear proofing your food is one of the basics of backcountry cooking. Now you know how to do it.",
